<title>GERMANY: Zeitler-no longer need for mark correction.</title>
<headline>Zeitler-no longer need for mark correction.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler said on Tuesday there now exists no need for major currencies to correct against the mark.</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters, Zeitler said &quot;the need for the mark to correct against major currencies from where it stood in 1995 and 1996 has in the meantime passed.&quot;</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
